Example 5.3 Consider the power set ring defined in Example 4.6. Using C = {1, 2, 3}
we have ℘ (C) = {∅, {1}, {2}, {3}, {1, 2}, {1, 3}, {2, 3}, {1, 2, 3}} as our ring. Define the set
S = {∅, {1}, {2}, {1, 2}}. The proof that S is a subring of ℘ (C) is an exercise at the end
of the chapter. The distinct cosets of S in ℘ (C) are shown next. Remember U ⊕ V =
(U − V ) ∪ (V − U ) for U, V ∈ ℘ (C).
